   6:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  * async-vs-sync split, sequential queue with dedupe and the isLoading gate,
   7:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  * the 16ms re-schedule, cache-entries-are-bitmap-or-false, stall recovery in
   8:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  * update(), and the exact placeholder-card painter.
   9:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *
  10:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  * C mapping of the Lua control flow:
  11:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *   - decodeRawImageData's async branches (JPEG/PNG/GIF/WebP) schedule a
  12:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *     tasks_run() whose single step performs the decode; onDone/onError map
  13:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *     1:1 onto Tasks.run's onComplete/onError, including the isDecoding flag.
  14:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *   - The sync branches (BMP/ICO/SVG) decode inline (pcall ≈ NULL check).
  15:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *   - processNextImage's playdate.timer.performAfterDelay(16, …) re-schedule
  16:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *     uses the project's pdtimer framework (P4), which fires on the first
  17:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *     frame update after the delay — the same observable pacing.
  18:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *   - The heavy decoders keep their Tasks.yieldCheck() call sites as
  19:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *     documented comments (the P24–P29 architecture: the task layer owns the
  20:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  *     frame budget; the decode completes inside one step on device).
  21:Source/render/image_decoder.c ****  */
